Positive structural checks: both project declarations present exactly once at
  their approved solution paths; no PackageReference/FrameworkReference/
  EmbeddedResource/Content in the production project; the 2025 policy exists
  only in SupportedExtractionTaxYears (no other production file hardcodes the
  year in executable code); Wave-0 CLAUDE.md content and pointer-only AGENTS.md.
Deliberate design choices:
  - Solution assertions are presence-and-uniqueness, never a total project
    count. A total count is what blocked this spec's own Wave 0 (see PR #66)
    and would block spec 008; this task does not re-lay that trap.
  - Comment lines are excluded from token scans. Documentation legitimately
    names forbidden concepts while explaining why they are forbidden; scanning
    raw text would make honest comments unwritable.
Anti-vacuity measures:
  - a guard test asserts the scanner sees all 8 production files and that a
    known-present pattern matches, so a broken file walk fails loudly rather
    than making every forbidden-pattern assertion pass for free
  - mutation-checked: injecting DateTime.UtcNow, RecipientIdentifier, the CRA
    line number 10100, a double, and a T5 type name into a production file
    fails exactly 5 boundary tests. Reverted before commit.
